{"name":"Kyanite","hex":"#1560fb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kyanite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blue neosilicate mineral, Al2SiO5, found in metamorphic rocks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kyanite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kyanite","blocks":[{"text":"Kyanite is a typically blue aluminosilicate mineral, found in aluminium-rich metamorphic pegmatites and sedimentary rock. It is the high pressure polymorph of andalusite and sillimanite, and the presence of kyanite in metamorphic rocks generally indicates metamorphism deep in the Earth's crust. Kyanite is also known as disthene or cyanite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Kyanite_crystals.jpg/330px-Kyanite_crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyanite","wikidata":"Q193450"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Kyanite.JPG/500px-Kyanite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Kyanite.JPG/1280px-Kyanite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Kyanite.JPG/500px-Kyanite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Deep blue kyanite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKyanite.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Kyanite_within_quartz%2C_as_collected_by_Dr_John_Hunter%2C_Hunterian_Museum%2C_Glasgow.jpg/500px-Kyanite_within_quartz%2C_as_collected_by_Dr_John_Hunter%2C_Hunterian_Museum%2C_Glasgow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Kyanite_within_quartz%2C_as_collected_by_Dr_John_Hunter%2C_Hunterian_Museum%2C_Glasgow.jpg/1280px-Kya